{
  "dom_id": "step-q108696",
  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "$\\frac{1}{7}\\,(-f)$ is equivalent to",
  "worked_solution": "First, remember that the product of a positive number and a negative number is a negative number. Thus, \n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{7}(-f)=-\\frac{1}{7}f.\n$$\n\nNow, writing $f$ as $\\frac{f}{1},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{7}f & =-\\frac{1}{7}\\cdot f \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{7}\\cdot \\frac{f}{1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1\\cdot f}{7\\cdot 1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{f}{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the expressions $\\frac{1}{7}(-f)$ and $-\\frac{f}{7}$ are equivalent.",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
